!.env.*.example

# xlsx/ is the working-data folder. Around 104 of its files are in no commit, branch or
# archive ref, so git cannot recover them. On 2026-09-05 a `git clean -fd` in the primary
# deleted four of them in one burst - a contract and three logo assets - because they were
# untracked but NOT ignored, while the 100 spreadsheets beside them survived precisely
# because `*.xlsx` above made them ignored. `git clean` skips ignored files, so this line
# extends that same protection to everything in the folder.
#
# The `/*` form is deliberate: `xlsx/` would exclude the directory itself, and git cannot
# re-include a file whose parent directory is excluded. This way a specific file can still
# be tracked with a negation below.
#
# It does NOT stop `git clean -fdx`, which overrides ignore rules by design, and it does
# not affect the six files already tracked in xlsx/.
xlsx/*

# ...and the one file in there that is CODE rather than output is tracked on purpose. A COPY of
# `scripts/field-day/print-day.mjs` sat at this exact path from 2026-10-03, ignored and therefore
# invisible, until it was 453 lines stale and a hand-run would have reprinted the defects #5573 and
# #5574 had just fixed. It is now a thin launcher with no logic in it; tracked, any edit that puts
# logic back shows up in `git status` and in review instead of waiting to be discovered on paper.
!xlsx/field-day-print.mjs
!xlsx/field-day.mjs

