# An `.env.<thing>.example` is a TEMPLATE and holds no value — `.env.analytics.example` has been
# tracked since the analytics box, and `.env.headwind.example` documents the device-management one.
# The negation at the top of this file is shadowed by the two `.env*` lines that follow it, so it is
# repeated here, last, where it actually wins. It stays narrow on purpose: only `.example`.
!.env.*.example
.vercel

# Next.js regenerates this on every dev/build and rewrites its import target
# depending on which one ran last:
#   next dev   -> import "./.next/dev/types/routes.d.ts"
#   next build -> import "./.next/types/routes.d.ts"
# Tracking it therefore left every worktree permanently "modified" with a file
# whose own header says "This file should not be edited" (6 of 7 dirty worktrees
# in the 2026-07-31 audit differed by nothing else), and one `git commit -a` away
# from committing whichever variant the last command happened to produce.
# Verified safe to untrack on 2026-07-31: `pnpm run typecheck` passes with the
# file absent, on a COLD tsbuildinfo, with no .next present — this tsconfig's
# `include` already covers `.next/types/**` and `.next/dev/types/**`, so the
# reference directives were redundant. Next recreates it on dev/build/typegen.
next-env.d.ts

# Output of the recruitment CV-ops scripts (scripts/recruitment-*.ts). Every file in
# here is a plan or a report about REAL job applicants — names, phone numbers,
# LinkedIn URLs, professional summaries — so it must never enter git history, where
# deleting it later does not remove it. The scripts write here by default and take
# CV_REREAD_OUT_DIR to write elsewhere.
.cv-reread/

# The CV cabinet fill script's resume ledger — machine-local, never shared.
.cv-cabinet-ledger.json
cabinet-build.log

# The 2026-09-21 Claude session recovery, consolidated into the repo folder at the owner's
# instruction. 5,092 files / 237 MB: a verbatim copy of the desktop app's per-account session
# store, 1,629 saved file versions, and the catalogues rebuilt from them. It is a COPY — the
# master stays at `F:\Claude Recovery 2026-09-21`, deliberately outside any git tree, because a
# `git clean -fdx` overrides ignore rules by design and this folder is not recoverable from
# history. The readable record is committed as `docs/recovery-2026-09-21.md`; the payload is not,
# and must not be: 237 MB of per-session JSON would sit in this repository's history forever.
claude-recovery-2026-09-21/

# One-off deliverables that sessions write to the repo ROOT and nobody ever commits: the
# per-line field-day sheets (`field-day-CNS.html`, `field-day-Summary-for-the-CEO.html`, …) and
# the per-person day cards (`nada-abdullah-day-card-2026-10-05.html` and its rendered `.pdf`).
# Seven of them sat untracked in the primary on 2026-10-06, which is what the app's diff pane was
# reporting as pending work on `main` when there were no tracked changes at all. They are NOT
# repository content: they are generated for one person or one line on one day, and a copy of
# every one already lives outside any git tree in `F:\Claude Scratchpad Archive\html\<date>\` and
# `…\pdf\<date>\` (the owner's never-delete rule covers HTML and PDF, so ignoring them here loses
# nothing). The leading `/` is deliberate — it scopes each pattern to the repo root, so a
# genuinely tracked sheet under `docs/` or `public/` is untouched; verified on 2026-10-06 that no
# tracked file in this repository matches either pattern.
/field-day-*.html
/field-day-*.pdf
/*-day-card-*.html
/*-day-card-*.pdf

# The same class, three more shapes, added 2026-10-07 at the owner's instruction after the app's
# diff pane reported `+1,073 -0` pending on `main` with no tracked change at all — the whole
# count was three untracked HTML deliverables sitting at the root: a per-person period card
# (`hassan-elsherbiny-period-card-2026-10-01-to-06.html`, 172 lines), a role handbook
# (`production-planner-handbook-2026-10-06.html`, 609) and a per-person guide
# (`sahar-khalil-production-planner-guide-2026-10-06.html`, 292), each beside its rendered
# `.pdf`, which the pane counts as 0 lines because it is binary. Generated for one person or one
# role on one day, archived outside every git tree by the never-delete rule, never repository
# content. Leading `/` again, so `docs/` and `public/` are untouched; verified 2026-10-07 that no
# tracked file anywhere in this repository matches any of the six.
/*-period-card-*.html
/*-period-card-*.pdf
/*-handbook-*.html
/*-handbook-*.pdf
/*-guide-*.html
/*-guide-*.pdf

# And the policy sheets the same generator writes beside them, added 2026-10-07 in the same
# clean-up: `phoenix-incentive-and-salary-policy-2026.pdf` and
# `phoenix-pedia-incentive-and-salary-policy-2026.pdf`. These two were the only root files the
# diff pane still listed after the six patterns above landed — binary, so 0 lines, but still two
# entries of noise on a checkout with no tracked change. The `.html` half is here for the same
# reason it is on every pair above: these PDFs are rendered FROM an HTML sheet, so the next run
# drops both. Root-scoped, and verified 2026-10-07 that no tracked file matches either.
/phoenix-*-policy-*.html
/phoenix-*-policy-*.pdf

# The session hand-off notes sessions drop at the root (`_handoff-crm-batch-2.md`,
# `_handoff-turbify-mailbox-ops.md`, …). Added at the owner's instruction on 2026-10-06, in the
# same breath as the two patterns above. They are one session's notes to the next, never
# repository documentation — anything that belongs to the repo goes in `docs/`, which this
# pattern cannot reach because of the leading `/`. Unlike the deliverables above these are
# Markdown, so the never-delete rule does not cover them and nothing archives them: they simply
# stay on disk, untracked and unlisted. Verified on 2026-10-06 that no tracked file matches.
/_handoff-*.md
